From ceb1b1ec8eda0b128581c568e0e7363b43c0f717 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 00:14:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] glm_moe_dsa: prompt chunks in two halves, exchanges under
 compute

A prompt chunk of 2,048 rows or more on the reduce-scatter path runs as
two halves of rows: each half's mixer and ffn on the main stream, each
site's exchange of one half on the side stream over a second NCCL
communicator (ncclCommSplit at start, three ranks or more), so one half's
exchange runs under the other half's compute and the main stream's own
collectives (the index split's gathers) never queue behind it. The second
half attends to the first half's keys of the same layer. Each half keeps
its own partial room, token lists and residual rows.
TF_GLM_DSA_HALVES=0 keeps whole chunks.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UQVvNktFCvQrvpNUbqtqBX
